## Library UI — do not freeze

Opening a project, Library, or a large folder must stay interactive.

- Call `Library.BeginBusy("Loading…")` **before** any await. `IsBusy` is ref-counted (`BeginBusy` / `EndBusy`).
- Progress: `PrgStartup` until the main shell is shown, then `PrgLibrary` on Library and `PrgProjectLoad` under the project combo. Bind Library bars to `IsBusy`. A freeze with no bar is a bug.
- Startup: activate the window **before** `InitializeAsync` / `LoadInitialDataAsync` (`App.OnLaunched` → `Window.Activate` → init → `ShowMain` → load). Do not await a full catalog load on a blank process.
- Status: `Loading…` → `Showing 80 of 2400` → the final count line.
- Project switch (`AppServices.SetCurrentProjectAsync`): bar first, Library, then Tags/Rooms/Settings. Tags mosaic is project-scoped.
- DB access: `PalaceDb.ReadAsync` / `WriteAsync` run the work on a thread-pool thread (`Task.Run`) while holding the single-connection gate, so `CatalogService` queries never execute on the UI thread. They take an optional `CancellationToken` (cancels the gate wait / a not-yet-started run, not work already inside SQLite). There is no sync `Read` / `Write` — never block on the gate. The `work` lambda runs off the UI thread: no `UiDispatch`, XAML, or `ObservableObject` mutation inside it, and no nested `ReadAsync` / `WriteAsync` (deadlock on the gate). Callers resume on their own context, so UI mutations after an await still go through `UiDispatch` when you are on a background thread.
- Folder browse: `GetAssetsAsync(folderPrefix:)` — do not load the whole project and filter in process. Folder grouping (source or nested prefix) runs on that prefix result (`FolderGroups`), not a whole-catalog in-process filter. Mosaic sort is the same query’s `ORDER BY` (`MosaicSortOrder.OrderBySql`); all-library and tag-browse mosaics also re-query instead of sorting `_allAssets` in process.
- Build `AssetItem`s off the UI thread. Chunk-append ~80 (`MosaicChunkSize`) on the dispatcher and `UiDispatch.YieldAsync`. Honor `_filterEpoch`.
- Mutate `Assets` only on the UI thread (`UiDispatch`). After chunks, `JustifiedMosaicLayout.Relayout` (`MosaicChunkAppended`). WASDK 2.4 `Layout.InvalidateMeasure` is protected — do not call it from LibraryPage.
- `ToItem` → `AssetItemMapper.FromAsset`. Never `File.Exists` or `ImageDimensions.TryRead` on the **original** while building the mosaic. Use stored Width/Height or a default aspect.
- Lazy thumbs: bind `ThumbImage`, not a static `FileToImage` during measure. Decode only through `ThumbLoadQueue` / `ThumbScheduler` (cap 2–4 by core count). Visible slots first, top-to-bottom then left-to-right, then a prefetch band (`PrefetchBandDip`). Cancel passes the job `CancellationToken` into `EnsureThumbnailAsync`, `DecodeCappedBgraAsync`, and `StillDecode`. The key leaves the cap as soon as it is abandoned (`CancelOutstanding` on mosaic reset) so a slow EXR/PSD/HDR does not block the next visible tile. A late complete with the old ticket is ignored. Thumbnail replace (`ThumbFileReplace`) catches `UnauthorizedAccessException` / `IOException` and keeps the existing JPEG. Tags and Rooms use `DecodeCappedSourceAsync`, not `FileToImage` / `UriSource`. Tags holds slots in `ThumbSlotGate`: cancelling the tile token frees the slot before `EnsureThumbnailAsync` returns, and a stale slot does not assign `ThumbImage`. EXR, Radiance, and scRGB scale poll that token. Decode size is the slot in DIPs times rasterization scale, fitted inside that box (`FitDecodeSize`). Pixel decode runs off the UI thread; only the finished `WriteableBitmap` is assigned on the dispatcher. Do not set `BitmapImage.UriSource` to the original still. In-memory LRU (`ThumbMemoryCache`) plus the on-disk JPEG. Do not start `StorageFile` work during measure. Timing log: LocalState `thumb-timing.txt` (`ThumbTimingLog`) — queue depth, per-thumbnail decode ms, preview decode ms, cache hit vs decode, capped preview, and `library-show page=reused` when returning from Settings.
- Library page `NavigationCacheMode` is `Required`. A Settings return must reuse the page. `Loaded` may run again when the page re-enters the tree; that path must not call `UpdatePreview` or `UpdateOverlayMedia` (no second full-res still). Side preview calls `DecodeCappedBgraAsync` for the preview box at the current scale and assigns the finished bitmap. A still larger than that cap, or an unknown size, uses the disk thumb when the file exists. Missing thumb still scale-decodes; it does not point `UriSource` at the original.
- `ItemsView` may not set `DataContext` on tiles and recycled containers do not re-fire `Loaded`. Stamp `Tag="{x:Bind MosaicTag, Mode=OneWay}"` on the `ItemContainer` (Id for tiles, `folder-group:` + path for headers) **and** `Tag="{x:Bind Id, Mode=OneWay}"` on the tile `Image`. Track live `Image`s and re-resolve via `GalleryMedia.FindAssetId` / `MatchesMosaicKey` on Tag / DataContext / chunk — do not untrack just because `DataContext` is not an `AssetItem`. Folder headers resolve through that mosaic key so tap / Open still navigates when Id and DataContext are empty.
- Overlay open is **double-click / Enter / Space / context Open** (Library and the Tags mosaic). **Esc** closes. **No single-click open.** Library `GrdAssets` keeps `IsItemInvokedEnabled=True` with `SelectionMode` Single/Multiple so ItemInvoked fires for double-tap, Enter, and UIA **InvokePattern** — not a single pointer tap (`ItemsView.CanRaiseItemInvoked`). Space opens the focused or selected tile (`GalleryScale.OpensOverlay` / `GalleryMedia.ShouldOpenOverlayFromSpace`); it does not toggle Select mode (click/tap still do). While overlay / GalleryWindow is open, do not mark Space handled on the viewer root (`GalleryScale.PassesViewerSpace`) — MediaPlayer play/pause and focused chrome use it; mosaic is a sibling so Space does not bubble there. Overlay close is **Esc** only. Do not synthesize a second click from `PointerPressed` on both the tile and `GrdAssets` — the same press arrives twice and opens on a single click. Do not open overlay from a header double-click or Space (`ShouldOpenOverlayFromDoubleTap` / `ShouldOpenOverlayFromSpace`): the first tap already navigates, and the second click can land on a new tile after the async mosaic reload. Overlay / GalleryWindow **backdrop** is in-app Acrylic (`GalleryOverlayBackdropBrush` in `App.xaml`) plus a light Smoke dim (`GrdGalleryBackdrop`) so the library blurs and darkens behind the still or video. Do not cover `MediaPlayer` transport; keep Info / Details. `GalleryWindow` uses `DesktopAcrylicBackdrop` (the blur of the library/desktop) plus **one** 0.28 Smoke layer — do not fill `GrdGalleryWindow` with Smoke and do not stack `GalleryOverlayBackdropBrush` on top (in-app acrylic only samples the window, so a full smoke fill hides desktop acrylic and double-dims).
- Library mosaic packing is `MosaicRows` / `JustifiedMosaicLayout`: folder headers are compact full-width caption rows (`FolderHeaderHeight`); assets keep justified tile rows. Wire both `MosaicReset` and `MosaicChunkAppended` to `Relayout()`. `GalleryMedia.MosaicAspectCount` still caps requested ranges; headers do not use asset-tile aspect.
- `AssetItem.ContentHash` is required for lazy generate and viewport upgrade. Do not recover the hash from the JPEG file name.
- Overlay image/video sources are applied in code-behind (`UpdateOverlayMedia`). Do not rely only on nested `x:Bind` of `OverlayGallery.CurrentPath` through a converter — that path is null until `LoadCurrentAsync` finishes and often never refreshes.
- Thumb generate stays viewport-ordered via the queue, never on the measure pass, skip `IsOnlineOnly` and shell-thumb stills (AVIF/HEIC/PSD). Do not replace `ThumbImage` when the cached JPEG is already decoded (folder-switch flicker). Reuse decoded bitmaps from `ThumbMemoryCache` by path and decode size. Never `ImageDimensions.TryRead` the original to decide regenerate.
